# docs/examples/receiver-sharing-a-radio-with-linbpq: the receiver on the radio's sound card,
# tuning the radio itself and holding a real LinBPQ off with XMITOFF, hearing the bench's
# stand-in for M0LTE. The radio is a Hamlib dummy rig left on the packet dial, 7.050100 MHz.
# LinBPQ's port 2 is a stand-in KISS TNC that keys that rig for every frame it is handed and
# writes down where the dial was; LinBPQ sends its ID every minute.
RECEIVER=$X/receiver-sharing-a-radio-with-linbpq/receiver.json
RIGS="listener:4532:7050100:USB:2400"
KISS_TNC=8100:4532
LINBPQ=$B/stand-in/bpq32.cfg
AIR="--tx $R/tx.out@7052300 --rx alsa:plughw:CARD=Loopback,DEV=0,SUBDEV=$SUB@rig:127.0.0.1:4532"
RUN_MINUTES=14
